 "result": "Ben Okafor has spent **\u20ac165.00** in total. That comes from two orders in the database:\n\n| Order | Item | Date | Total (EUR) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 3 | Keyboard | 2026-09-02 | 120.00 |\n| 8 | Mouse | 2026-08-19 | 45.00 |\n| | **Total** | | **165.00** |\n\nThe shop's `customer_total` tool gave a different answer, **\u20ac410.00**, and the database doesn't support it. When I checked:\n- There is only one customer named Ben Okafor (id 2).\n- No orders point to a customer that doesn't exist, so none are going uncounted.\n- 410 doesn't match any customer's total. It isn't the total of all orders either, which is \u20ac477.\n\nI can't see how `customer_total` works out its number. Until someone checks it, I'd go by the database figure and not that tool.",
